    <td width="510" class="main_copy" valign="top">
<h3>Capability & Qualifications</h3><br />
<p>CommuniCare staff members have an <i><b>extensive history</b></i> of success 
in a number of community intervention, prevention, juvenile justice, substance 
abuse and organizational development areas as well as nonprofit management 
programming. The agency has staff members who have doctoral and masters degree 
training and competencies in these areas as well as effective bachelors prepared 
staff who are very strong in the delivery of skill building, case management, 
community collaboration and training. Some areas of competence include:</p>
<ul><li>Behavior assessment and intervention planning including specific skill 
	building in youth and adolescents</li><li>Systems of Care collaboration and intervention</li><li>Clinical and management supervision training/team development</li><li>Care coordination and community support for at-risk/high risk youth</li><li>Wrap-around intensive services programming for the highest-risk juvenile 
	court youth</li><li>Substance abuse treatment involving adolescents and court-involved youth 
	/ families</li><li>Evidence-based substance abuse prevention programming</li><li>Positive youth development and youth leadership</li><li>Conference planning, management and strategic implementation</li><li>Grant writing and program development</li><li>Program implementation, monitoring, program evaluation, data analysis 
	and reporting</li><li>Quality management and quality improvement</li><li>Nonprofit management and organizational development</li><li>Training and skill development in a wide array of topics (see
	<a href="http://www.cccommunicare.org/Training%20Files.htm" mce_href="http://www.cccommunicare.org/Training%20Files.htm" target="_blank">Selected Training Workshops 
	Provided by Staff</a>)</li></ul>
<p>Clients or contracts served by CommuniCare, Inc. over the years include:</p>
<ul><li>County of Cumberland</li><li>North Carolina Department of Juvenile Justice and Delinquency Prevention/State 
	of NC</li><li>NC Governor's Crime Commission</li><li>Cumberland County Schools</li><li>Cumberland County Community Development</li><li>U.S. Department of Justice and Substance Abuse Mental Health Services 
	Administration</li><li>United Way of Cumberland County</li><li>Cumberland Community Foundation</li><li>City of Fayetteville<ul><li>and a number of smaller grants and foundation relationships</li></ul>
	</li></ul><br /><br /></td>
